    { "id": "ford-get-scouted-tips", "authority": "first_party_published", "publisher": "Ford Models, Inc.", "url": "https://www.fordmodels.com/get-scouted", "title": "Get Scouted | Ford Models", "locale": "en", "retrievedOn": "2026-08-19", "locator": { "kind": "section", "value": "FORD's Tips to Getting Scouted" }, "excerpt": "We don't want to see you in your fanciest outfit with lots of makeup on. We are looking for you at your most natural. Have a clean face with absolutely no makeup. Pull your hair back. Wear a form fitting outfit like skinny jeans and a tank top. We need to see the shape of your body.", "archivedUrl": null, "contentHash": null },
    { "id": "ford-privacy-children", "authority": "first_party_published", "publisher": "Ford Models, Inc.", "url": "https://www.fordmodels.com/privacy-policy", "title": "Privacy Policy | Ford Models", "locale": "en", "retrievedOn": "2026-08-19", "locator": { "kind": "section", "value": "What are our policies regarding children?" }, "excerpt": "Registrants must be eighteen (18) years of age or older in order to independently submit an Application to us. Registrants may be under eighteen (18) years of age if their parent/legal guardian registers on their behalf; however, Registrants may in no case be under thirteen (13) years of age.", "archivedUrl": null, "contentHash": null },
    { "id": "ford-recruitment-warning", "authority": "first_party_published", "publisher": "Ford Models, Inc.", "url": "https://www.fordmodels.com/get-scouted", "title": "Get Scouted | Ford Models", "locale": "en", "retrievedOn": "2026-08-19", "locator": { "kind": "section", "value": "Recruitment Warning" }, "excerpt": "You should never pay to attend a casting. You should never share photos in the nude or in lingerie. All FORD Models representatives correspond via email domains that end with fordmodels.com.", "archivedUrl": null, "contentHash": null }
  ],
  "review": { "authority": "agency_branded_provider", "method": "dual_reviewer", "reviewers": [{ "id": "spec-registry-rebuild-lane-20260819", "reviewedOn": "2026-08-19" }, { "id": "normalization-review-20260829", "reviewedOn": "2026-08-29" }], "notes": "Revision 2 replaces the channel this series named. Revision 1 described the Snapcast form, and the 2026-08-19 research established that fordmodels.com/get-scouted mounts the Snapcast embed for Paris only: New York, Chicago, Los Angeles, Miami and Barcelona all mount one shared selectroom.app form, and a New York applicant never reaches the Snapcast form through Ford's own site. Everything downstream of that changes with it - four differently named slots, two of them required rather than four requested, JPEG and PNG rather than a format left unpublished, and no size cap where revision 1 carried 3MB. The 3MB figure was not wrong when it was recorded; it belongs to the Paris route. The circulating 600KB-total and 25MB-video figures match nothing on either form: this one has no size cap in its markup or its copy and no video field at all. Paris is not published as a series. Its form is a different application - it creates an account, adds inseam, collar and shoe fields, and asks for four uploads whose labels render as the string undefined - and its accept string was never captured, which is the open research gap this revision does not paper over. The age rules come from Ford's privacy policy, which is the only published age statement and is dated May 2018; the form contradicts it by accepting a birth year of 2016 with no guardian step, and the unknown carries that. Slot labels carry the shot name without the form's required-marker asterisk, which `modality` already states and which would otherwise reach the README a talent hands an agency. Two facts are recorded here rather than in the rules: the close-up upload carries a Portrait only badge and nothing else about orientation is published, and the Get Scouted page states that every Ford representative writes from an address ending in fordmodels.com - an anti-impersonation claim that belongs to the verification layer. Open calls are published per city and change often; at the observation date only Chicago was holding them, Mondays to Thursdays 2pm to 3pm." }
}
